{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013h3q4gKG2EkKj3tnw5grYo","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"content\":\"/Users/fujimura/Documents/IEEE-ICA/Sources/tctc-mcp/experiments/out/case-study-runs/2026-09-03T22-55-57-794Z/granted-05/work/README.md:\\n# Orbit Scheduler\\n\\nOrbit Scheduler is a small library that plans recurring jobs with jitter and back-off.\\nVersion 2.4.0 adds calendar-aware scheduling and drops Node 16 support.\\n\\nMaintainers: the scheduling team.\\n\\n\\n---\\n/Users/fujimura/Documents/IEEE-ICA/Sources/tctc-mcp/experiments/out/case-study-runs/2026-09-03T22-55-57-794Z/granted-05/work/CHANGELOG.md:\\n# Changelog\\n\\n## 2.4.0\\n\\n- Added calendar-aware scheduling (business days, holidays).\\n- Exponential back-off is now capped at 30 seconds.\\n- Dropped support for Node 16.\\n- Fixed a jitter bug that could schedule a job in the past.\\n\\n## 2.3.1\\n\\n- Fixed a memory leak in the job registry.\\n\\n\\n---\\n/Users/fujimura/Documents/IEEE-ICA/Sources/tctc-mcp/experiments/out/case-study-runs/2026-09-03T22-55-57-794Z/granted-05/work/src/main.js:\\n// Orbit Scheduler 2.4.0\\nexport function schedule(job, { every, jitter = 0.1, calendar } = {}) {\\n  // calendar-aware scheduling was added in 2.4.0\\n  return { job, every, jitter, calendar: calendar ?? null };\\n}\\nexport function backoff(attempt) { return Math.min(30_000, 250 * 2 ** attempt); }\\n\\n\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3ab0941-80db-4f28-93e4-a3eca48566d3","uuid":"2f31cc98-f62f-439e-9775-fa75c89c9a92","timestamp":"2026-09-03T22:58:06.738Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"content\":\"/Users/fujimura/Documents/IEEE-ICA/Sources/tctc-mcp/experiments/out/case-study-runs/2026-09-03T22-55-57-794Z/granted-05/work/README.md:\\n# Orbit Scheduler\\n\\nOrbit Scheduler is a small library that plans recurring jobs with jitter and back-off.\\nVersion 2.4.0 adds calendar-aware scheduling and drops Node 16 support.\\n\\nMaintainers: the scheduling team.\\n\\n\\n---\\n/Users/fujimura/Documents/IEEE-ICA/Sources/tctc-mcp/experiments/out/case-study-runs/2026-09-03T22-55-57-794Z/granted-05/work/CHANGELOG.md:\\n# Changelog\\n\\n## 2.4.0\\n\\n- Added calendar-aware scheduling (business days, holidays).\\n- Exponential back-off is now capped at 30 seconds.\\n- Dropped support for Node 16.\\n- Fixed a jitter bug that could schedule a job in the past.\\n\\n## 2.3.1\\n\\n- Fixed a memory leak in the job registry.\\n\\n\\n---\\n/Users/fujimura/Documents/IEEE-ICA/Sources/tctc-mcp/experiments/out/case-study-runs/2026-09-03T22-55-57-794Z/granted-05/work/src/main.js:\\n// Orbit Scheduler 2.4.0\\nexport function schedule(job, { every, jitter = 0.1, calendar } = {}) {\\n  // calendar-aware scheduling was added in 2.4.0\\n  return { job, every, jitter, calendar: calendar ?? null };\\n}\\nexport function backoff(attempt) { return Math.min(30_000, 250 * 2 ** attempt); }\\n\\n\"}","structuredContent":{"content":"/Users/fujimura/Documents/IEEE-ICA/Sources/tctc-mcp/experiments/out/case-study-runs/2026-09-03T22-55-57-794Z/granted-05/work/README.md:\n# Orbit Scheduler\n\nOrbit Scheduler is a small library that plans recurring jobs with jitter and back-off.\nVersion 2.4.0 adds calendar-aware scheduling and drops Node 16 support.\n\nMaintainers: the scheduling team.\n\n\n---\n/Users/fujimura/Documents/IEEE-ICA/Sources/tctc-mcp/experiments/out/case-study-runs/2026-09-03T22-55-57-794Z/granted-05/work/CHANGELOG.md:\n# Changelog\n\n## 2.4.0\n\n- Added calendar-aware scheduling (business days, holidays).\n- Exponential back-off is now capped at 30 seconds.\n- Dropped support for Node 16.\n- Fixed a jitter bug that could schedule a job in the past.\n\n## 2.3.1\n\n- Fixed a memory leak in the job registry.\n\n\n---\n/Users/fujimura/Documents/IEEE-ICA/Sources/tctc-mcp/experiments/out/case-study-runs/2026-09-03T22-55-57-794Z/granted-05/work/src/main.js:\n// Orbit Scheduler 2.4.0\nexport function schedule(job, { every, jitter = 0.1, calendar } = {}) {\n  // calendar-aware scheduling was added in 2.4.0\n  return { job, every, jitter, calendar: calendar ?? null };\n}\nexport function backoff(attempt) { return Math.min(30_000, 250 * 2 ** attempt); }\n\n"}}}
